Each file under csrc/ is a DISTILLATION of a KernelForge campaign source: the
accepted kernel plus its one accepted configuration, with the search space that
produced it removed.  It is NOT a verbatim copy and cannot be re-synced by
copying -- a kernel update is a re-distillation, gated on the campaign's
integration suite reproducing its three results unchanged: the 8-check gate and
shape suite, bit-exact equivalence against the standard path at every verify
batch shape, and ~41.2 us for the fused four-kernel chain in graph replay.

  csrc/dual_gemv_bf16.cu   cfg 61 of 67          <- bench/csrc/dual_gemv_bf16.cu
  csrc/indexer_qk_had.cu   impl 3, 1 of 3 kernels <- bench/csrc/indexer_qk_had.cu
  csrc/logits_kernel.hip   variant 20 of 80      <- experiments/phaseC/logits_kernel.hip
  csrc/topk_phaseD.cu      1 of 5 kernels        <- experiments/phaseD/topk_phaseD.cu

